  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sub Dialogue 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Now that the relation between each token is represented in this QUERY/KEY embedding,
    we can use it to scale the VALUE embedding based on how much each of the tokens
    is affected by the other tokens in the sequence.
  - However, we will need to clean up the numbers a bit before we do that!
  - The multiplication might have enlarged certain numbers so much that they would
    trump the more subtle influences of other components. To fix this, we SCALE the
    numbers down based on the dimensions of the embedding.
  - Next, we apply another ACTIVATION function called a SOFTMAX. The SOFTMAX function
    scales each number so they keep their ratios, but add up to 1. This is great
    to represent percentages, which works well in this use case!
